"Salesforce will operate as the SAML Service Provider (SP), while Idira/CyberArk Identity will operate as the SAML Identity Provider (IdP), authenticate the user using a phishing-resistant passkey, and issue the SAML response to Salesforce."

they normally do not each require a different SP Entity ID merely because they're different Salesforce accounts.

One SAML SP configuration can authenticate multiple Salesforce users since its still under 1 SF Org



